Shield up, rope paying out, you follow the three sets of boots around the bend. The gallery opens into a wider working, an old stope with square timber props and a low, sagging roof. A pile of rubble lies against the far wall. The three prints cross the room and go on; the fourth man's staggering return comes back through the same space, and in the middle of the floor the dust is scuffed and churned, as though men had milled about there and then turned suddenly.

The three sets of boots leave the far side of the stope and vanish into a darker gallery that runs on downward. The rope behind you is still paying out true.


